---
title: LOG - logging backends
---
%% ON-CHIP ONLY as far as wiring goes - LOG is a software layer.
%% The UART sink is the one that leaves the chip: USART1 on PA9/PA10 reaches
%% the ST-LINK virtual COM port, so no extra cable is needed.
%% log_error and friends are macros that capture __FILE__ and __LINE__.
flowchart LR
    subgraph APP["Application"]
        CALL["log_error / log_warn / log_info / log_debug"]
    end

    subgraph LOGC["LOG core"]
        LVL["Level filter"]
        FMT["log_format - timestamp, level, file:line"]
    end

    subgraph SINKS["Sinks"]
        UARTS["log_sink_uart"]
        PRINTF["log_sink_printf - semihosting or SWO"]
    end

    subgraph OUTP["Where it lands"]
        VCP["USART1 PA9/PA10 to ST-LINK VCP"]
        TERM["Serial terminal at 115200 8N1"]
        SWO["SWO / debugger console"]
    end

    CALL --> LVL
    LVL --> FMT
    FMT --> UARTS
    FMT --> PRINTF
    UARTS --> VCP
    VCP --> TERM
    PRINTF --> SWO
